  "rationale": "All three listed models are direct matches to urolithiasis via aligned endpoints around “Calculus of kidney and ureter” / nephrolithiasis. PGS001250 is explicitly a pan-trait UK Biobank framework score (“Significant sparse polygenic risk scores across 813 traits...”) with a sparse snpnet model and is therefore penalized on study archetype despite having reported PRS-only metrics; its endpoint is also time-to-event, which is a noted warning signal for generic disease risk. PGS004493 and PGS004563 are siblings from the same (non-pan-trait) publication with the exact same ICD-style endpoint (N20) and ancestry context, but they lack comparable discrimination metrics (AUC/R² are null) and have unknown covariates, limiting certainty. Between those siblings, PGS004563 has the stronger reported per-SD effect size (OR 1.283 vs 1.227), so it is the best-supported choice within the most endpoint-faithful, non-framework cluster; however, the absence of PRS-comparable performance metrics keeps this from being a high-confidence/high-quality direct selection."
